          "question": "Tired all the time for a couple of months, and my periods have been heavy.",
          "answer": "Feeling tired for a couple of months, along with heavy periods, is worth raising with a doctor or nurse. Your description did not match any emergency pattern in the guidance I searched. That does not rule out a serious cause, so get medical advice promptly if your symptoms become severe, get worse, or feel new and unexplained.\n\nThe only retrieved guidance that mentions both symptoms is the **Hypothyroidism** summary (General clinical reference). It lists fatigue and heavy or irregular periods among the slowly developing symptoms of an underactive thyroid. It also says these symptoms are common in people without thyroid disease. A diagnosis is usually confirmed with repeated blood tests, not from symptoms alone.\n\nThe search did not cover other possible causes of tiredness with heavy periods, so I can't tell you what else might explain it. A clinician can ask about your periods and other symptoms and decide which tests, if any, are needed. It may help to keep a note of when the tiredness and heavy bleeding started, how often you change pads or tampons, and any other changes you've noticed.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
